# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in REAL values. `.env` is git-ignored.
# Claude Code expands ${VAR} placeholders in .mcp.json from your shell env,
# so `export` these (or `source .env`) before launching `claude`.

# ── GitHub MCP (remote, HTTP) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fine-grained or classic Personal Access Token.
# Scopes for read-only repo/PR/issue work: `repo`, `read:org`.
GITHUB_PAT=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Atlassian Rovo / Jira MCP (remote, HTTP) ─────────────────────────────────
# The jira server in .mcp.json uses OAuth 2.1 (browser-based) — NO secret needed
# here. On first use, run `/mcp` inside Claude Code and authenticate jira in the
# browser; Claude Code stores the OAuth token for you.
#
# (Optional) If you ever switch back to headless API-token auth, set the jira
# entry's Authorization header to "Basic ${ATLASSIAN_AUTH_B64}" and provide:
#   ATLASSIAN_AUTH_B64=$(echo -n "you@example.com:YOUR_API_TOKEN" | base64)
# Note: API-token mode exposes only Teamwork Graph tools (no JQL search), so the
# "last 5 bugs" query requires OAuth.
